  "Suite récurrente par l'étude complète de f (problème long)": "Recursive sequence through a complete study of f (long problem)",
  "Étudier f, comparer son graphe à y = x, puis discuter la suite selon a₁.": "Study f, compare its graph with y = x, then discuss the sequence according to a₁.",
  "C'est le problème de 13 points de l'examen MT. On étudie f (dérivées, extrema, convexité, asymptotes), on compare son graphe à la droite y = x, puis on discute la suite selon a₁.<br>L'idée clé : un extremum local de f qui est aussi un point fixe <b>borne</b> la suite.": "This is the 13-point problem of the MT exam. Study f (derivatives, extrema, convexity, asymptotes), compare its graph with the line y = x, then discuss the sequence according to a₁.<br>The key idea: a local extremum of f that is also a fixed point <b>bounds</b> the sequence.",
  "aₙ₊₁ = aₙ + (2 + aₙ)/(1 + aₙ) : L = L + (2 + L)/(1 + L) donne L = −2": "aₙ₊₁ = aₙ + (2 + aₙ)/(1 + aₙ): L = L + (2 + L)/(1 + L) gives L = −2",
  "(a) Seule limite possible": "(a) The only possible limit",
  "f′(x) = 1 − 1/(1 + x)² = x(x + 2)/(1 + x)², f″(x) = 2/(1 + x)³ ; max local f(−2) = −2": "f′(x) = 1 − 1/(1 + x)² = x(x + 2)/(1 + x)², f″(x) = 2/(1 + x)³; local max f(−2) = −2",
  "(b) Étude de f": "(b) Study of f",
  "f(x) > x ⇔ x < −2 ou x > −1": "f(x) > x ⇔ x < −2 or x > −1",
  "(c) Position par rapport à y = x": "(c) Position relative to y = x",
  "a₁ < −2 : croissante, majorée par −2 (le max de f sur ]−∞ ; −1[) ; a₁ > −1 : → +∞": "a₁ < −2: increasing, bounded above by −2 (the max of f on ]−∞ ; −1[); a₁ > −1: → +∞",
  "(d) Discussion": "(d) Discussion",
  "La suite converge (vers −2) si et seulement si a₁ < −1": "The sequence converges (to −2) if and only if a₁ < −1",
  "le signe de f(x) − x et les points fixes": "the sign of f(x) − x and the fixed points",
  "dérivées, convexité et asymptotes de f": "derivatives, convexity and asymptotes of f",
  "Bissection et méthode du point fixe (cours MT)": "Bisection and the fixed-point method (MT course)",
  "Garder la moitié où f change de signe ; g contractante.": "Keep the half where f changes sign; g contracting.",
  "<b>Bissection</b> : on coupe [a ; b] en son milieu m et on garde la moitié où f change de signe ; après n étapes, l'erreur est ≤ (b − a)/2ⁿ.<br><b>Point fixe</b> : si g([a ; b]) ⊂ [a ; b] et |g′| ≤ k < 1 sur [a ; b], la suite xₙ₊₁ = g(xₙ) converge vers l'unique point fixe de g.": "<b>Bisection</b>: cut [a ; b] at its midpoint m and keep the half where f changes sign; after n steps, the error is ≤ (b − a)/2ⁿ.<br><b>Fixed point</b>: if g([a ; b]) ⊂ [a ; b] and |g′| ≤ k < 1 on [a ; b], the sequence xₙ₊₁ = g(xₙ) converges to the unique fixed point of g.",
  "f(x) = x³ + x − 1 sur [0 ; 1] : f(0) = −1 < 0, f(1) = 1 > 0": "f(x) = x³ + x − 1 on [0 ; 1]: f(0) = −1 < 0, f(1) = 1 > 0",
  "m = 0,5 ; f(0,5) = −0,375 < 0 : on garde [0,5 ; 1]": "m = 0,5; f(0,5) = −0,375 < 0: keep [0,5 ; 1]",
  "Étape 1": "Step 1",
  "m = 0,75 ; f(0,75) ≈ 0,1719 > 0 : on garde [0,5 ; 0,75]": "m = 0,75; f(0,75) ≈ 0,1719 > 0: keep [0,5 ; 0,75]",
  "Étape 2": "Step 2",
  "Erreur ≤ 1/2ⁿ ≤ 10⁻³ dès que n ≥ 10 (2¹⁰ = 1024)": "Error ≤ 1/2ⁿ ≤ 10⁻³ as soon as n ≥ 10 (2¹⁰ = 1024)",
  "Nombre d'étapes": "Number of steps",
  "g(x) = 1/(1 + x²) : g([0 ; 1]) ⊂ [0 ; 1] et |g′(x)| ≤ 0,65 < 1": "g(x) = 1/(1 + x²): g([0 ; 1]) ⊂ [0 ; 1] and |g′(x)| ≤ 0,65 < 1",
  "Point fixe contractant": "Contracting fixed point",
  "chaque moitié gardée contient un zéro (TVI)": "each kept half contains a zero (IVT)",
  "|g′| ≤ k < 1 rend g contractante (accroissements finis)": "|g′| ≤ k < 1 makes g contracting (mean value theorem)",
  "Rayon de convergence et domaine, bornes comprises": "Radius of convergence and domain, endpoints included",
  "ρ par d'Alembert, R = 1/ρ, puis chaque borne à part.": "ρ by the ratio test, R = 1/ρ, then each endpoint separately.",
  "Pour Σ aₙ(x − x₀)ⁿ, d'Alembert sur |aₙ| donne ρ = lim |aₙ₊₁/aₙ|, et <b>R = 1/ρ</b> (R = +∞ si ρ = 0). La série converge absolument pour |x − x₀| < R et diverge pour |x − x₀| > R.<br><b>Les deux bornes x₀ ± R s'étudient à part</b> : ce sont des séries numériques.": "For Σ aₙ(x − x₀)ⁿ, the ratio test on |aₙ| gives ρ = lim |aₙ₊₁/aₙ|, and <b>R = 1/ρ</b> (R = +∞ if ρ = 0). The series converges absolutely for |x − x₀| < R and diverges for |x − x₀| > R.<br><b>The two endpoints x₀ ± R are studied separately</b>: they are numerical series.",
  "d'Alembert": "ratio test",
